---
import AtlasLayout from '../layouts/AtlasLayout.astro';
import release from '../data/release';
---
<AtlasLayout title="Sources">
  <section class="page-width content-page">
    <p class="eyebrow">Evidence provenance</p><h1>Trace every claim.</h1><p class="hero-description">Primary studies, trial reports and official status sources are linked to individual claims. Each record identifies the inspected source location, study system and limitations.</p>
    <aside class="preview-notice"><span class="notice-symbol" aria-hidden="true">i</span><div><strong>Source checks are recorded; domain review is pending</strong>Many checks are limited to primary-report abstracts. This bounded candidate does not claim exhaustive literature coverage, independent replication or human approval.</div></aside>
    <ul class="source-list">{release.sources.map(source => <li id={source.id}><span class="record-label">{source.kind.replaceAll('_',' ')}</span><h2><a href={source.url}>{source.title}</a></h2><p>{source.citation}</p><p>Study identity: {source.studyId}. Inspected: {source.accessScope}.</p><p>Linked evidence items: {release.evidenceItems.filter(evidence => evidence.sourceId === source.id).length} · Source checks: {[...new Set(release.evidenceItems.filter(evidence => evidence.sourceId === source.id).map(evidence => evidence.retrievedAt))].join(', ')}.</p><ul>{release.evidenceItems.filter(evidence => evidence.sourceId === source.id).map(evidence => { const claim = release.claims.find(item => item.evidenceItemIds.includes(evidence.id)); return claim && <li><a href={`/diseases/sle/#claim-${claim.id}`}>{claim.text}</a></li>; })}</ul></li>)}</ul>
    <h2>Source selection</h2><p>Trial publications and status reports are kept distinct. A trial's multiple claims share a study identity and are not counted as independent replication. Regulatory approval is scoped to the recorded US indication. The enpatoran sponsor announcement establishes development status, not efficacy.</p><p>A retracted 2002 BLyS/APRIL paper was excluded; the IFN-α–BLyS link instead uses the directly relevant 2014 SLE monocyte report. The candidate includes limitations and negative primary trial endpoints where identified.</p><p><a href="/methodology/#publication-policy">Read the scientific publication policy</a> · <a href="/diseases/sle/#mechanism-outline">Inspect all claims</a></p>
  </section>
</AtlasLayout>
